{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_tidal_conservatories","title":"The Glass Tide","logline":"When junior tide-warden Mara Ilek discovers the Glassgate Locks are silting shut ahead of schedule, she must persuade a wary barge pilot and a proud guild master to halt the firing season and dredge the channels before the spring tide can no longer power the city.","theme":"A city survives when its people share both evidence and the work it demands.","acts":[{"id":"act_setup","title":"The Early Silt","purpose":"setup","scenes":[{"id":"scn_mara_finds_silt","title":"Soundings Before Schedule","summary":"At the Glassgate Locks, Mara compares fresh settle lines with her earlier surveys and finds the sills filling weeks ahead of schedule. She records the evidence in her mother's precise hand, but the numbers alone offer no plan for winning the guilds' cooperation.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek"],"goal":"Confirm whether the lock sills are silting faster than the tide tables predict.","conflict":"Mara trusts her measurements, but fears that reporting them will make her seem like the alarmist the guilds called her mother.","outcome":"The soundings confirm early silting, and Mara decides the channels must be checked independently before the spring tide."},{"id":"scn_sana_sets_terms","title":"A Bargain for the Barge","summary":"Mara asks Sana to carry her through the channels for a second survey. Sana agrees only if the cooperative has a say in who keeps the fertile silt, forcing Mara to confront the rights dispute instead of treating it as a detail.","location_id":"loc_algae_fields","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Secure Sana's barge and channel-reading for an independent survey.","conflict":"Sana needs fair payment and a voice in silt rights; Mara wants the survey underway without making promises she cannot keep.","outcome":"Mara agrees to bring Sana's terms to the wardens, and Sana commits her barge to the survey.","depends_on":["scn_mara_finds_silt"]}]},{"id":"act_rising_action","title":"A Season at Stake","purpose":"rising_action","scenes":[{"id":"scn_barge_confirms_depth","title":"Depth by the Tiller","summary":"Sana pilots the barge along the gate channels while Mara takes soundings. Sana feels the shallows through the tiller, and the two methods agree: the channels are filling faster than the official survey allowed for.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Establish evidence strong enough to justify dredging before the spring tide.","conflict":"Mara's measurements require careful interpretation, while Sana's barge cannot safely linger in the shallowing channel.","outcome":"Their independent readings match, giving Mara corroboration and Sana grounds to demand a fair dredging contract.","depends_on":["scn_sana_sets_terms"]},{"id":"scn_pell_refuses_closure","title":"The Calendar Holds","summary":"At Bellmaker's Quay, Mara presents the paired readings to Pell and asks him to stop the firing season. Pell pursues his promise to protect the guild's work, dismisses the junior warden's case, and refuses to shorten the calendar even though he recognizes what the tide tables imply.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Win Pell's agreement to close the gates for dredging before the spring tide.","conflict":"Pell's guild depends on a full firing season, and his pride prevents him from admitting that Mara's evidence may be right.","outcome":"Pell keeps the calendar unchanged; Mara realizes that evidence without a shared plan will not move the guild.","depends_on":["scn_barge_confirms_depth"]},{"id":"scn_silt_terms_brought_forward","title":"The Commons' Silt","summary":"At the Mangrove Terraces, Mara and Sana trace how dredged silt can restore the root-gardens, as it did after the Great Silting. Sana argues that the cooperative must be paid and included; Mara acknowledges the silt-debt rule and commits to putting both obligations into a public dredging plan.","location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Build a dredging proposal that respects both the silt-debt rule and the cooperative's claim to fair terms.","conflict":"Sana distrusts the wardens' charter, while Mara has no authority to settle the dispute alone.","outcome":"They agree on a proposal: the cooperative will dredge under a contract, and the recovered silt will be spread on the terraces within the season.","depends_on":["scn_pell_refuses_closure"]},{"id":"scn_pell_accepts_channel_test","title":"A Test at the Locks","summary":"Mara brings Pell the revised plan and asks him to inspect the channel before making his decision. Pell agrees to go, but insists the test must show whether the gates can remain open through the firing season.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_oren_pell","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Get Pell to assess the evidence at the locks alongside Mara and Sana.","conflict":"Mara needs Pell to face the risk, while Pell still frames the inspection as a chance to defend the full season.","outcome":"Pell joins them aboard Sana's barge, creating a direct test of the choice he has avoided.","depends_on":["scn_silt_terms_brought_forward"]}]},{"id":"act_climax","title":"The Gate Must Close","purpose":"climax","scenes":[{"id":"scn_test_at_spring_channel","title":"The Channel's Answer","summary":"At the Glassgate Locks, Mara reads the settle lines as Sana pilots the shallows. Pell hears the measurements and sees how little margin remains before the spring tide; keeping the gates open for the full season would gamble the tide that powers the city.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Determine whether the gates can stay open through the firing season without risking the spring tide.","conflict":"Pell wants to protect the guild's season, but the combined soundings and channel depth make his preferred calendar unsafe.","outcome":"Pell accepts that dredging cannot wait and agrees to close the gates, provided the cooperative's work and silt terms are honored.","depends_on":["scn_pell_accepts_channel_test"]},{"id":"scn_guild_halts_firing","title":"A Season Recast","summary":"At Bellmaker's Quay, Pell announces a halt to firing so the locks can be dredged before the spring tide. Mara presents the shared plan instead of relying on her numbers alone, and Sana secures the cooperative's contract and a clear route for the silt to reach the terraces.","location_id":"loc_bellmakers_quay","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro","chr_oren_pell"],"goal":"Turn Pell's decision into an agreed closure, dredging contract, and silt plan.","conflict":"Pell risks his standing by ending the season early, while Sana will not let the cooperative's labor be separated from its rights.","outcome":"The guild halts firing, Sana commits the barge, and the gates are scheduled to close for dredging before the spring tide.","depends_on":["scn_test_at_spring_channel"]}]},{"id":"act_resolution","title":"The Tide Returns","purpose":"resolution","scenes":[{"id":"scn_silt_spread_terraces","title":"The Debt Returned","summary":"After the locks are dredged, Sana hauls the fertile silt to the Mangrove Terraces and ensures it is spread within the season. Mara helps coordinate the work, turning the silt-debt rule into a visible benefit for the people who shared the cost of reopening the channels.","location_id":"loc_mangrove_terraces","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Carry the dredged silt to the terraces and fulfill the silt-debt obligation.","conflict":"The cooperative must move the silt promptly while ensuring its labor and rights are not forgotten once the emergency passes.","outcome":"The silt enriches the root-gardens, and Sana's cooperative is recognized as a partner in keeping the lagoon working.","depends_on":["scn_guild_halts_firing"]},{"id":"scn_tide_restored","title":"A Shared Sounding","summary":"At the Glassgate Locks, Mara checks the cleared sills as the spring tide enters the lagoon. Pell stands with her rather than defending the old calendar, and Sana's barge waits in the channel; the city's tide-powered life continues because each of them helped hold the gate.","location_id":"loc_glassgate_locks","character_ids":["chr_mara_ilek","chr_oren_pell","chr_sana_duro"],"goal":"Verify that the reopened gates admit the spring tide safely.","conflict":"Mara must trust a shared effort rather than her own records alone, and Pell must live with the season he chose to sacrifice.","outcome":"The tide passes through the cleared locks, Pell accepts a shorter season as the price of the lagoon's future, and Mara has learned to carry proof into partnership.","depends_on":["scn_silt_spread_terraces"]}]}]}
</Output>
